0..72 Comment "//! `spiders` models a sort that carries a special commutative Frobenius"
73..129 Comment "//! algebra, and a circuit rule whose wires merge on it."
130..133 Comment "//!"
134..212 Comment "//! The spiders of an orthonormal basis copy and merge its states. Without the"
213..279 Comment "//! mark, the lowering refuses each such merge at its shared port."
280..283 Comment "//!"
284..360 Comment "//! `@[ frobenius ]` marks the sort `Q`. The rule `merge` writes no node for"
361..439 Comment "//! the merge: its wire map repeats the name `z`. The lowering reads the merge"
440..517 Comment "//! as a spider and decides the rule as a diagram, modulo the Frobenius laws."
518..521 Comment "//!"
522..623 Comment "//! - see: corpus/pathological/circuit/spiders-unmarked.gandr — the same rule over an unmarked sort"
624..688 Comment "//! - cites: [Coecke-Kissinger-2017-picturing_quantum_processes]"
689..692 Comment "//!"
693..839 Comment "//! [Coecke-Kissinger-2017-picturing_quantum_processes]: https://doi.org/10.1017/9781316219317 \"Coecke and Kissinger, Picturing Quantum Processes\""
841..917 Comment "/// `Qubit` marks its sort, so a circuit rule may merge and split its wires."
